+
+### `applyPatch(document, patch)`
+
+Applies a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) (RFC 6902) to a JSON `document` and
+returns the resulting document as a new value, without mutating `document`.
+
+- `document`: any JSON-compatible value.
+- `patch`: an array of operations, each an object with an `op` of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,
+  `copy` or `test`, a `path` (a JSON Pointer), and a `value` (`add`/`replace`/`test`) or `from` (a JSON
+  Pointer, for `move`/`copy`).
+
+Throws a `JsonPatchError` if `patch` is not a syntactically valid JSON Patch, or if one of its
+operations fails to apply (e.g. a `path`/`from` that doesn't resolve, a `test` whose `value` doesn't
+match, or a `move` whose `from` is a proper prefix of its `path`).
